-- two reports about one molecule with different values: no single-valued function of the molecule agrees
-- with both. So a record that holds disagreeing notifications cannot be read as a hazard of the
-- substance at all, which is the Classification and Labelling Inventory's situation — the entries are
-- grouped for the same substance and the agency does not verify them. The resolutions are the two the
-- regulation actually uses: an authority that overrides (the harmonised entry of Annex VI) or the
-- warrants kept distinct, each report carrying whose assessment it is.
reports-disagree-no-function : (M : Mol) → (r1 : Report Nat) → (r2 : Report Nat) → rep-mol Nat r1 ≡ M → rep-mol Nat r2 ≡ M → (rep-value Nat r1 ≡ rep-value Nat r2 → Empty) → ((h : Mol → Nat) → ((r : Report Nat) → h (rep-mol Nat r) ≡ rep-value Nat r) → Empty)
reports-disagree-no-function M r1 r2 q1 q2 no =
  λ h → λ agrees → no (concat (sym (agrees r1)) (concat (cong h q1) (concat (cong h (sym q2)) (agrees r2))))
